n: 3.8.2
name: miniature
kind: hub
is: mini-nums is 687 lines of Python that intern blueprint and recipe trees under four-integer ids in arrival order. Nothing evaluates a recipe or holds a value. All 7 tests (15 assertions) pass; one compares a constant with itself and two assert only counts. Probes show names outside identity, field order inside, and rebinding that moves only a name.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-nums-study-2023

n: 3.8.2.1
name: mini-id-scheme
kind: observation
is: A mini-nums id is four integers (package, level, type, instance) printed P.L.T.I, with package 1 everywhere. A composite's level is max(child levels, category level) + 1, floored at 3. A minted id is 1.<level>.<category type>.<entries + 1>: an arrival-order ordinal per level, keyed by the string of category id and child ids joined with '+'.
status: observed
src: 2.16.5#92-107 2.16.5#138-149 2.16.5#158-183
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-nums-study-2023

n: 3.8.2.2
name: mini-differs-from-numsgo
kind: observation
is: mini-nums departs from NUMS.Go in six places: package is 1 for catalogue and minted ids (NUMS.Go: 0 and 1); a minted id carries the category's type (NUMS.Go: 0); literal tables are per module (per recipe); objects are structural (nominal); blueprint children carry no edge bitmask; an unresolved name raises NameError (NUMS.Go auto-declares).
status: observed
src: 2.16.5#183 2.16.5#197-199 2.16.5#236-242 2.16.6#120 2.16.8#50 2.16.25#3 2.16.25#4 2.16.1#3.1
limit: The NUMS.Go side of the package, type, literal and unresolved-name rows rests on the first-round core report and on one run of a scratch build.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-nums-study-2023

