n: 3.8.4.2
name: struct-and-ctor-ids-differ
kind: observation
is: A dump of NUMS.Go on a file with 'type A struct{x, y int}' and 'type B struct{p, q int}' gives A blueprint 1.3.0.1 and B 1.3.0.2, both storing 0.2.2.3+0.1.2.2^0+0.1.2.2^0; 'var g1 = 5' and 'var g2 = 5' get constructor recipes 1.3.0.2 and 1.3.0.4. The README of the folder nums-go-2023 says each such pair shares one id.
status: observed
src: 2.16.1#6 2.16.2#95-97 2.16.13#272-274 2.16.13#719-721 2.16.14#69-72 2.16.14#82-85
why: Should_Reserve is true for object, interface, package and function declarations; a reserved entry is stored as value=key, so a lookup by value never finds it, and Update_Entry then overwrites it in place. The two constructor bodies differ in the access leaf, 0.1.13.1 against 0.1.13.2.
limit: One run of the first-round scratch build of NUMS.Go (four build lines removed, upstream grammar in place of the absent fork); the binary and its output were in a session scratch directory.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-nums-study-2023

