n: 3.8.8.2
name: rebinding-moves-a-name
kind: finding
is: Make name rebinding a stated rule: binding a name again points the name at a new node and leaves every existing node in place. mini-nums behaves so as a side effect, and the rule agrees with axiom 3 and its reversibility theorem, under which undo is re-pointing a name at a blueprint that is still referenced.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.8.2.8 1.3 1.7.8
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-nums-study-2023

n: 3.8.8.3
name: decide-field-names-in-identity
kind: finding
is: Decide consciously whether field names and field order enter a blueprint's identity. In mini-nums field names are outside identity and field order is inside, so {x, y} and {p, q} are one shape; NUMS.Go stores the same child string for two such structs and separates them only by nominal reservation. Neither reference states the consequence.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.8.2.8 3.8.4.2
