n: 3.8.9.4
name: same-shape-same-id-across-languages
kind: finding
is: Drop 'same shape, same id, across languages, for free'. Two Go structs of one shape get different ids in NUMS.Go, no handler exists for a second language, and the one mini-nums test that claims identity across two surfaces is a tautology. Nothing in NUMS.Go or in the folder nums-go-2023 puts a second programming language or any natural language through its store; the old body does both (3.10.1.3, 3.11). The quoted words paraphrase README.md line 127.
